truth_text:
Structured Contents pulls infoboxes, sections, tables, citations, references, images and more out of raw wikitext and HTML and returns it as machine-readable JSON. No custom parser or regex needed. On the left is what an article's wikitext looks like in regular payloads. On the right is the parsed infobox extracted from that wikitext, easily usable in Structured Contents payload. "{{Short description|American-born French entertainer (1906–1975)}}
{{Other people}}
{{Use American English|date=January 2026}}
{{Use mdy dates|date=June 2026}}
{{Infobox person
| name = Josephine Baker
| image = File:Baker Harcourt 1940 2.jpg
| caption = Baker in 1940
| birth_name = Freda Josephine McDonald
| birth_date = {{birth date|mf=yes|1906|06|03}}
| birth_place = [[St. Louis]],
